# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Voice Conversation — configuration
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. With no .env at all, the app runs end to end on
# the fakes: a scripted STT, a canned LLM, and a silent TTS. That is the default
# on purpose — clone the repo, `pnpm install && pnpm dev`, and the whole loop
# works with no accounts, no keys, and no spend. The test suite and CI never read
# these values.
#
# Set the keys below only when you want to hear real audio.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Pipeline selection (a DEFAULT, not the authority) ----------------------
# The browser picks providers per session from dropdowns in the UI; these set
# what a session *starts* as. Keys decide what the UI is allowed to offer — a
# stage with no key shows its real option greyed out.
#
# Asking here for a provider whose key is missing makes the server refuse to
# start. Falling back silently is how a deployment ends up serving fakes to real
# users while its health check stays green.
#   STT_PROVIDER:  fake | deepgram
#   LLM_PROVIDER:  fake | anthropic
#   TTS_PROVIDER:  fake | fake-silent | deepgram
#
# These are the criterion-7 swap: changing a value here must require no change to
# @voice/core. The brief defines the demonstration as running "once with a real
# provider and once with the silent fake", so `fake-silent` is the other side of
# the swap — no second paid vendor is needed.
#
# `fake` TTS is an audible tone rather than silence, so the demo can be checked by
# ear with no keys at all.
STT_PROVIDER=fake
LLM_PROVIDER=fake
TTS_PROVIDER=fake

# --- Deepgram (STT: Nova-3, TTS: Aura-2) -----------------------------------
# One key covers both. https://console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic (the model) --------------------------------------------------
# https://console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which Claude a session STARTS on. The browser's Model dropdown overrides this
# per session, so treat it as the opening position rather than the setting.
#
# Haiku is the default deliberately. In a voice loop you hear silence until the
# first clause reaches the synthesiser, so time-to-first-word is felt directly in
# a way that raw capability is not — a better answer that starts a second later is
# usually the worse conversation. Measured on a short prompt:
#
#   claude-haiku-4-5    ~1.4 s to first token   (default — fastest)
#   claude-sonnet-4-6   ~1.6 s
#   claude-sonnet-5     ~1.4 s
#   claude-opus-5       ~2.5 s                  (most capable, audibly slower)
#
# Anything not on that list falls back to the default rather than being forwarded
# to the API — the same list is a whitelist on the server, because the value can
# also arrive from the browser.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# --- Server ----------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8787
HOST=0.0.0.0

# Where the built browser app is served from, so one origin serves both the page
# and the WebSocket. Defaults to apps/web/dist relative to the server module,
# which is correct for `pnpm dev` and for the container alike — set it only if you
# relocate the build. Unset with no build present is fine: the server logs that it
# is running API-only rather than serving a blank page.
# WEB_DIST=
